Python + 7 non-Python).\n\nWI-pisab-furis (Level 2) shipped in full on 2026-04-23 across four PRs (#3313, #3315, #3316, #3317, #3318):\n- NameMatcher utility and matcher-boundary canonicalization patterns are live and language-agnostic.\n- AST-walking lint converts containment from convention to enforcement.\n- ADR-0028 stabilized the pass criterion (`edge.is_resolved == True` with an evidence_type drawn from `evidence_types_on_axis(AXIS_INFERENCE_PATHWAY)`).\n- The polyglot call-site coverage fixture exists FOR PYTHON ONLY. Each non-Python language needs its own fixture file authored using the Python file as the template before the audit can run on it.\n\nImplementation path per non-Python language (iterative, half-day each):\n1. Author the fixture file (~5 idiomatic import × call constructs for that language) using the Phase 4 Python fixture as a template.\n2. Run the property test; misses surface as failing assertions.\n3. If misses surface: file a per-language analyzer-fix WI item (sibling shape: WI-dulun / WI-bunul / WI-dadid)."  # 9a89
